WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.801
We are here with Adam Sandler!

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.400
Well, let's talk
"Murder Mystery 2,"

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.901
'cause I think
this is gonna be giant.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.868
But it's you
and Jennifer Aniston.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.767
The first one was like
the biggest --

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.200
I think it was the most
popular thing on Netflix.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.834
-Of that year it was, yeah.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.634
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.167
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Just to say that is crazy.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.267
-That feels good.
-We love Jennifer Aniston.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:25.267
-Great young lady.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.934
-You guys have
a great chemistry.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.067
-Love her very much.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.601
I know Jennifer
since we're very young.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.567
I was 22.
She was 20.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.801
I met her at a delicatessen.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.167
She was with
a good friend of mine.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.634
They were hanging out.
I sat down.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.067
She had eggs.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.834
I was eating French toast.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.400
-You have a really good memory.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.100
-Well, I remember
everything, yes.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.133
I had chocolate milk
that morning.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.400
And a crazy straw.
-Holy moly.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.901
I can't believe
you remember all this.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.601
-I didn't finish it.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:58.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.434
-I can't believe you remember
all these details.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.734
-I blew bubbles.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.868
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:07.033
-I want to talk about this
because this is the sequel.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.033
You guys are now
a detective agency.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.868
-Yes, we're a married couple.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.767
We have -- We quit --

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.934
Last movie, we did pretty well,

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:18.234
and we figured out some crimes,
right, some "moi-ders."

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:22.534
And we figured out
who "moi-derlized" everybody.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.667
"You moi-dered me."

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:28.200
And then this movie,
Jennifer quit her job

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.067
as a --
she worked at a hair salon.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:35.934
I quit my job as a cop, and we
become detectives together.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:38.200
It's not going well.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.200
We are not very good at it.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.100
Then the maharaja
from the first movie

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.100
invites us to his wedding,

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.701
and turns out
the maharaja gets kidnapped.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.567
Can you believe it?

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.701
So guess what.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.634
Jennifer and I
try to solve who did it.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:57.367
-Oh, yeah!

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.701
It's bigger.
It's action-packed.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.400
-It is.
-It is global.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.367
This one is massive. Dude.
-Yes.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.968
-Eiffel Tower thing --
Am I spoiling something?

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:10.901
-No. Jennifer falls off
the Eiffel Tower in it.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:12.634
-Yeah, but it's --

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.934
I read somewhere, like,
they've never even done a scene

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.334
on the top of the Eiffel tower
in the history of film.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:18.701
-It was very cool.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:19.868
They did it like
2:00 in the morning,

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.467
'cause when you go to Paris,

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.834
you go to to see
the Eiffel Tower.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.400
-Of course.
-So they were like,

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.200
"You can shoot there, but do it
at like 2:00 in the morning

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.501
so we're not ruining
everybody's time."

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.934
-They come to Paris. Yeah.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.467
-Yeah, so we shot at 2:00
in the morning,

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.501
and Jennifer's stunt girl,
Kelly,

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:37.901
she went out there
and swung on a rope.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:39.000
It was really cool.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.901
-From the top of the --
It's so great.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.467
It's cool to watch.
I know. Someone's like...

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:44.300
Yeah, it's great.
-Scary, scary.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.000
-The movie's fantastic.
I want to show a clip.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.467
Here's Adam Sandler
in "Murder Mystery 2."

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:49.934
Take a look at this.
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:52.601
-But what about the colonel?
What's his motive?

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:56.334
-Well, maybe he just is sick
of working for rich people

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.200
'cause you guys suck.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.667
Or maybe the colonel
needed enough money

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:06.968
to afford himself a bionic arm.

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:10.267
-I looked into it.
They're not very expensive.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.501
